1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
In Polytrade, describe a comparison in chat: three strategies, two take-profit values, and three holding limits. That creates eighteen combinations.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The agent queues a real background experiment. Open it to follow saved progress and access cancellation.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Rank candidates by return after costs, and inspect their exact settings. Here the leading breakout configuration still loses six point one four percent.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Ask for walk-forward validation in the same conversation. The full eighteen-combination grid is reused.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Five folds optimize on earlier training windows, then evaluate frozen settings on the next unseen window.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Only unseen test periods contribute to this equity curve. Returns, drawdown, trades, costs, and benchmarks remain visible.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Inspect each fold's dates and selected parameters. Positions close at the boundaries, while test cash carries forward. These are historical simulations.
